---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Sidebar from '../components/Sidebar.astro';
import Carousel from '../components/Carousel.astro';
import ContactForm from '../components/ContactForm.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="Ambotics™" description="A new robotics company. Coming soon.">
  <main id="top" class="min-h-screen w-full">
    <div
      class="mx-auto max-w-[1440px] px-6 sm:px-10 lg:px-[84px] pt-16 sm:pt-20 lg:pt-[104px] pb-24"
    >
      <!-- Single grid: sticky left sidebar (logo + nav) + content -->
      <div class="lg:grid lg:grid-cols-[340px_minmax(0,1fr)]">
        <Sidebar />

        <!-- Content column -->
        <div class="min-w-0 mt-14 lg:mt-0">
          <h1
            class="font-display ss01 max-w-[360px] text-[clamp(28px,5vw,32px)] font-medium leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink"
          >
            A new kind of robotics company.
          </h1>

          <div class="mt-14 lg:mt-20">
            <section
              id="starting"
              class="max-w-content space-y-10 body-copy text-[14px] leading-[1.4] tracking-[-0.02em]"
            >
              <p>
                Robotics has spent most of its life as a demonstration. Impressive in a
                lab, filmed in slow motion, explained in a language only engineers could
                follow, and almost never present in the rooms where real work actually
                gets done.
              </p>
              <p>
                Most companies in this field still build for the lab. They lead with the
                hardware and the breakthrough, and they speak to other engineers. We do
                the opposite. We lead with your business, in plain language, about your
                problem. If automating a task does not produce a real return for your
                operation, we will not take it on. That discipline is not a limitation.
                It is the whole promise.
              </p>
              <p>
                We own the entire stack: software, hardware, data, training, and model
                evaluation, so we can iterate faster than anyone else. When we do take
                something on, we own all of it. The hardware, the installation, the daily
                operation, and the support that keeps everything running long after the
                first day. You will never have to become a robotics expert or assemble a
                line of vendors to make it work. You show us where the repetitive work
                lives. We carry the rest.
              </p>
            </section>

            <Carousel />

            <section
              class="mt-24 max-w-content space-y-10 body-copy text-[14px] leading-[1.4] tracking-[-0.02em]"
            >
              <p>
                Most of our customers start in the same place. They have a sense that
                something in their operation could be done better, and they are not sure
                what is possible or where to begin.
              </p>
              <p>
                Tell us where the repetitive work lives. We will tell you plainly whether
                there is a case for automating it. If there is, we will build it, run it,
                and stand behind it.
              </p>
            </section>

            <ContactForm />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
